  {
   "tag": "3Gen",
   "h2": "Three Genders Again",
   "body_html": "<p><strong>Der</strong> Stift (m), <strong>das</strong> Buch (n), <strong>die</strong> Tafel (f). All German nouns are capitalised — even common ones like Stift (pen).</p>"
  },
  {
   "tag": "Cases",
   "h2": "Akkusativ Heads-Up",
   "body_html": "<p>When you HAVE something, the masculine 'der' becomes <strong>den</strong>: 'Ich habe einen Stift' (I have a pen). Don't worry too much yet — just notice it.</p>"
  },
  {
   "tag": "Bag",
   "h2": "In My Bag",
   "body_html": "<p>'In meiner Schultasche ist ein Buch und ein Lineal' = 'In my schoolbag is a book and a ruler'.</p>"
  }
 ],
